{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Thirteenth turn: CheckRun 4e8ef1701c7b4020a40640d1a7f2e4e2 (completed, exit_code 0) evaluates all five comparisons of the follow-up basis completely - the stale-decided case is violated again at witness index 9, and the four decision-formation comparisons hold (batched vector equality and index/content consistency at index 1, leader-change prefix preservation at index 3, recovery convergence at index 4). The two open decision-formation questions now receive accounts built on that receipt instead of remaining empty.\\\",\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"5d087c25407e4157b6b06176a649ef5c-question-0\\\",\n      \\\"experiment_id\\\": \\\"39f7d4c4c0484f7e94edbc51cbd78c2b-experiment\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower\\\", \\\"leader_accepted\\\", \\\"batching\\\", \\\"quorum\\\"],\n      \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"4e8ef1701c7b4020a40640d1a7f2e4e2\\\": [1]},\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"holds\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": null,\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Current account: in the exercised batched configuration the reported accepted index and the entries a node holds stay consistent. The harness admits the case (leader 3, follower 1, batch_size 4, 16 proposals) and then proposes eight entries on the leader and eight on a follower concurrently; when every node reports decided_idx 16, the comparison on the result event (receipt event index 1) shows all_logs_equal true, index_content_consistent true (for every node, the entry readable at index i is the element that node reports for index i) and all_values_present true over exactly the 16 proposed values. So the suspicion that a follower's batched append would report an accepted index that does not correspond to the entries it holds is not supported here: the leader's decide step, each follower's batched append and the index each node reports agree in this schedule. defect_claim is null because no defect judgment is made on this question; the counterevidence below records what this does not establish.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The check is a proxy: it verifies agreement of the decoded decided vectors and of the entry readable at each index, not the internal accepted-index number a follower puts into its Accepted reply, which is not exposed by the public API.\\\",\n        \\\"All 16 proposals were emitted before the cluster was pumped, so the case does not cover a follower receiving a batched AcceptDecide while the leader's decided_idx already exceeds the follower's accepted idx during the same exchange; the earlier local probe that did cover that path also agreed, but it is not a retained receipt.\\\",\n        \\\"Nothing in the case exercises compaction, so the index/content comparison is only valid while no prefix has been trimmed or snapshotted.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"One deterministic schedule of one configuration (three nodes, majority quorum, batch_size 4, no reconfiguration, no message loss).\\\",\n        \\\"Only the dev profile was exercised, as in every run of this session.\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"5d087c25407e4157b6b06176a649ef5c-question-1\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower_prepare\\\", \\\"leader_accsync\\\", \\\"logsync\\\", \\\"leader_promises\\\"],\n      \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"4e8ef1701c7b4020a40640d1a7f2e4e2\\\": [3, 4]},\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"conditional\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": null,\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Current account, scoped to what was measured: after a six-entry prefix is decided, removing the leader and electing a replacement among the survivors leaves the decided prefix unchanged on every surviving node (receipt event index 3, prefix_preserved true, all_logs_equal true, decided_everywhere true at decided_len 10), and rebuilding the removed leader from its persisted storage converges to the same decided vector as the survivors without altering the prefix (event index 4, recovered_caught_up true, recovered_prefix_preserved true, recovered_all_logs_equal true). So on the exercised leader-change and recovery path, LogSync/AcceptSync did not truncate or reorder decided entries. The account is conditional because the question also asks about the specific adoption branch where a promise reports a newer accepted round or a longer accepted log than the leader's: that branch is the one the stale-decided case exercises (follower handle_prepare taking the create_log_sync path from the preparing leader's decided index), and there the response aborts rather than adopting, which bounds but does not answer the general question for configurations where that request stays inside the responder's compacted prefix.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The measured case has the replacement leader elected among nodes that already agreed on the prefix, so the replacement's log was not shorter than the survivors' decided prefix; a leader with a genuinely shorter log adopting through a promise is not covered by these two comparisons.\\\",\n        \\\"No message loss, reordering or duplicate delivery is applied in this case, so the sequence-number and re-prepare repair paths are not exercised.\\\",\n        \\\"Neither case includes compaction, so the snapshot/delta branch of the log update is not exercised here.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"One deterministic schedule of one configuration (three nodes, majority quorum, batch_size 2).\\\",\n        \\\"The adoption branch that the question names is only partially covered, through the failing compaction interaction recorded under b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-question-0; no run in this session observed that branch completing outside the contrast case's snapshot-enabled configuration.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
